    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.input\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nWould it be reasonable to disable search highlight by default?\r\n\r\nTemporarily, I use:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal input = MiniInput.get({\r\n  handlers = {\r\n    view = MiniInput.gen_view.floatwin({\r\n      adjust_config = function(state, config)\r\n        local win = state.data.floatwin_win_id\r\n        if win then\r\n          vim.wo[win].winhighlight = vim.wo[win].winhighlight .. \",Search:MiniInputNormal\"\r\n        end\r\n        return config\r\n      end,\r\n    })\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.input</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Would it be reasonable to disable search highlight by default?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Temporarily, I use:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local input = MiniInput.get({\n  handlers = {\n    view = MiniInput.gen_view.floatwin({\n      adjust_config = function(state, config)\n        local win = state.data.floatwin_win_id\n        if win then\n          vim.wo[win].winhighlight = vim.wo[win].winhighlight .. &quot;,Search:MiniInputNormal&quot;\n        end\n        return config\n      end,\n    })\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">input</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniInput</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">get</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">handlers</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">view</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniInput</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_view</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">floatwin</span>({\n      <span class=\"pl-en\">adjust_config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">state</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">config</span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">win</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">state</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">data</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">floatwin_win_id</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">win</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n          <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">wo</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">win</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">winhighlight</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">wo</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">win</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">winhighlight</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>,Search:MiniInputNormal<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">config</span>\n      <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n    })\n  },\n})</pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.input\nQuestion\nWould it be reasonable to disable search highlight by default?\nTemporarily, I use:\nlocal input = MiniInput.get({\n  handlers = {\n    view = MiniInput.gen_view.floatwin({\n      adjust_config = function(state, config)\n        local win = state.data.floatwin_win_id\n        if win then\n          vim.wo[win].winhighlight = vim.wo[win].winhighlight .. \",Search:MiniInputNormal\"\n        end\n        return config\n      end,\n    })\n  },\n})",
