            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Would it be reasonable to disable search highlighting by default?\r\n\r\nI don't think this is a good idea. Personally, I find it often useful to have searched term highlighted in this type of special windows (input, picker, etc.). For example, it makes it easier to be sure that there is no typo or that the search is for something I'd expect.\r\n\r\nThe alternative is to make clearing the highlighting easier for the user, almost to the point of it being a habit. That is what `\\h` and (the new) `<C-c>` in 'mini.basics' are for.\r\n\r\nEspecially since there are workarounds, I'll close this as not planned.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Would it be reasonable to disable search highlighting by default?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't think this is a good idea. Personally, I find it often useful to have searched term highlighted in this type of special windows (input, picker, etc.). For example, it makes it easier to be sure that there is no typo or that the search is for something I'd expect.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The alternative is to make clearing the highlighting easier for the user, almost to the point of it being a habit. That is what <code class=\"notranslate\">\\h</code> and (the new) <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-c&gt;</code> in 'mini.basics' are for.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Especially since there are workarounds, I'll close this as not planned.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Would it be reasonable to disable search highlighting by default?\n\nI don't think this is a good idea. Personally, I find it often useful to have searched term highlighted in this type of special windows (input, picker, etc.). For example, it makes it easier to be sure that there is no typo or that the search is for something I'd expect.\nThe alternative is to make clearing the highlighting easier for the user, almost to the point of it being a habit. That is what \\h and (the new) <C-c> in 'mini.basics' are for.\nEspecially since there are workarounds, I'll close this as not planned.",
